02:43:17.390 --> 02:43:22.050
native to this environment, there is a risk
that you will become lost.

02:43:22.050 --> 02:43:32.370
And being lost could be an indescribably terrifying
experience, where the line between reality

02:43:32.370 --> 02:43:42.310
and what you might perceive as a hyper reality
in this other dimension, or fabricated reality

02:43:42.310 --> 02:43:48.899
as a UI, as we perceive it, versus any type
of objective truth, things can get very, very

02:43:48.899 --> 02:43:51.521
unclear very quickly.

02:43:51.521 --> 02:43:58.310
And I don't expect anyone to understand this
or even take it as reasonable that you could

02:43:58.310 --> 02:44:00.529
have that experience if you haven't been there.

02:44:00.529 --> 02:44:05.740
But take my word for it, you can get to some
very, very slippery terrain.

02:44:05.740 --> 02:44:11.160
Furthermore, I would say no matter how many
times you have done this, doesn't matter if

02:44:11.160 --> 02:44:19.819
it's 10, or a hundred, or 200, you always
stand the chance of pulling a joker card from

02:44:19.819 --> 02:44:25.310
the deck and getting your fucking ass handed
to you in a very serious way, that has lasting-

02:44:25.310 --> 02:44:26.310
Kevin Rose: Yeah.

02:44:26.310 --> 02:44:27.520
I don't want to do it anymore.

02:44:27.520 --> 02:44:28.680
I don't want to do it anymore.

02:44:28.680 --> 02:44:30.311
Tim Ferriss: That has lasting consequences.

02:44:30.311 --> 02:44:37.470
Now, I will say, just for you, Kevin, the
