02:45:20.311 --> 02:45:25.720
Things can get very strange, and they almost
certainly will get very strange.

02:45:25.720 --> 02:45:28.130
I have never had the experience...

02:45:28.130 --> 02:45:29.430
Actually, I take that back.

02:45:29.430 --> 02:45:35.220
Well, in my first few experiences, there were
one or two times where I felt out of control,

02:45:35.220 --> 02:45:40.950
fully out of control, and was completely dislocated
from anything resembling this reality.

02:45:40.950 --> 02:45:52.630
But generally speaking, now, or in recent
history, I can go through very, very, very,

02:45:52.630 --> 02:45:54.700
very challenging experiences.

02:45:54.700 --> 02:46:02.171
But if someone near me says, "Tim, are you
okay," or, "Tim, how are you doing," I can

02:46:02.171 --> 02:46:17.529
reply to that in perfectly coherent English,
even if I am, by all subjective interpretations,

02:46:17.529 --> 02:46:21.420
completely removed from time, space, identity.

02:46:21.420 --> 02:46:22.910
Kevin Rose: That's amazing.

02:46:22.910 --> 02:46:27.000
Tim Ferriss: I can still respond to that,
which is a developed...

02:46:27.000 --> 02:46:31.050
I think that's a cultivated skill, at least
for me.

02:46:31.050 --> 02:46:41.091
But the fact of the matter remains that I
could not have foreseen how violently I would

02:46:41.091 --> 02:46:46.750
be destabilized from that experience a year
and a half, two years ago.

02:46:46.750 --> 02:46:53.859
And I think that was in part due to a degree
of overconfidence, after many rounds for a

02:46:53.859 --> 02:46:55.520
non-clinician, for non-professional.

02:46:55.520 --> 02:47:00.910
The professionals drink four or five nights
a week and do so for years and years and years

02:47:00.910 --> 02:47:01.910
on end.

02:47:01.910 --> 02:47:07.260
So anyone who's like, "I've done ayahuasca
10 times, I understand ayahuasca," you are

02:47:07.260 --> 02:47:11.450
setting yourself up for spiritual head kick.

02:47:11.450 --> 02:47:17.300
Kevin Rose: The reason I'm excited about this,
and tell me if this is foolish, and I'm fine

02:47:17.300 --> 02:47:25.140
with you saying that; The one thing that I
really appreciate about this practice of meditation

02:47:25.140 --> 02:47:26.830
is that there's two things.

02:47:26.830 --> 02:47:31.260
One, it's Henry slaps his legs and he says,
"Just, this, just this.

02:47:31.260 --> 02:47:38.190
This is the moment, just this," and that really
snaps me back into this is the moment.

02:47:38.190 --> 02:47:44.120
And the second piece is that this idea of
surrender, where you have something that's

02:47:44.120 --> 02:47:50.040
facing you and you're like, "That's just a
thought, let's surrender back to the moment,"

02:47:50.040 --> 02:47:53.300
is a big piece of this practice.

02:47:53.300 --> 02:47:58.010
And do you think that either of those things
would be helpful in this, or is that just-

02:47:58.010 --> 02:47:59.010
Tim Ferriss: 100%.

02:47:59.010 --> 02:48:02.740
I'll tell you how they'll be helpful in my
experience and how they'll be a hindrance,

02:48:02.740 --> 02:48:05.090
or how they can be a hindrance.

02:48:05.090 --> 02:48:18.390
So, on the helpful side, in these very, let's
call them unusual and alternate experiences

02:48:18.390 --> 02:48:25.181
of reality in say an ayahuasca experience,
and you can have nothing nights also, by the

02:48:25.181 --> 02:48:26.181
way.

02:48:26.181 --> 02:48:29.020
You get a brew that's super weak, or you just
simply for whatever reason, have your body

02:48:29.020 --> 02:48:30.101
veto the experience.

02:48:30.101 --> 02:48:32.710
You can have null experiences.

